{"title":"Mean Value Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The Mean Value Theorem (often abbreviated MVT) is considered one of the most important results in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_analysis\" title=\"Real analysis\">real analysis</a>. An elegant proof of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fundamental_Theorem_of_Calculus\" title=\"Fundamental Theorem of Calculus\">Fundamental Theorem of Calculus</a> can be given using Mean Value Theorem. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mean_Value_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/212b2745cf32bdb4ace7d1a8510395ecc6aee0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:[a,b]\\rightarrow\\mathbb R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> be differentiable function on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Interval\" title=\"Interval\">interval</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. The <b>Mean Value Theorem</b> states there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f76e87bbf4a4f84ba42bf98c46d570c773d603b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be34c960742f6b639203c1c86c698c7dd2e81617.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f&#39;(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mean_Value_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4f7c7b319db780decfabc3d3800e1c687745c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" /> is the slope of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Secant\" title=\"Secant\">secant</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a> which passes through the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f211bdc3c819522d6db554f2aa43281147ace917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,f(a))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e7e4e9445cc4ee51a85405f9b9162c5da61047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,f(b))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad068e7351c7984460d96648477748648d8b7f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f(x)-\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}(x-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"268\" height=\"42\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is continuous on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> since it is the linear combinatoin of the continuous functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a90f61985f370451472515e737f23321e0256d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0c7ebe207e9b80b0ba88d5fac047820492481d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g&#39;(x)=f&#39;(x)-\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is differentiable on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/2608e9bb5cf407c510a334dafa3df28809c73c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)=g(b)=f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rolle%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Rolle&#39;s Theorem\">Rolle's Theorem</a>, there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f76e87bbf4a4f84ba42bf98c46d570c773d603b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e8f469d29a8c1d4be497fa51757f48e380a059.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g&#39;(c)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2335dc82cd2b1c1a1cf4185c2c5fcc630030ef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f&#39;(c)=g&#39;(c)+\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"38\" /> as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da7272b06f09b1f8f6b67d6d1b31a3261a4aabd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mean_Value_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017134703\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 86/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3838/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.894      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.894      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7008:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017134703 and revision id 228515. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}